inches) from 1901 to 2010. This is largely thought to be due to both glacier melt and thermal expansion of seawater. Thermal expansion means that as objects such as solids, liquids, and gases heat up, they expand in volume.","position":{"start":{"line":130,"column":1},"end":{"line":130,"column":1}},"key":"nNsrTHtjkK"}],"key":"SiR40MrIZ3"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":132,"column":1},"end":{"line":132,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"link","url":"https://slcc.pressbooks.pub/introgeology/chapter/15-global-climate-change/","position":{"start":{"line":132,"column":1},"end":{"line":132,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Text Source","position":{"start":{"line":132,"column":1},"end":{"line":132,"column":1}},"key":"OIpjonGgoI"}],"urlSource":"https://slcc.pressbooks.pub/introgeology/chapter/15-global-climate-change/","key":"MByzgZ1gjW"}],"key":"ejY7aSGxF3"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":134,"column":1},"end":{"line":134,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Global sea level has risen about 8 inches (0.2 meters) since reliable record-keeping began in 1880. By 2100, scientists project that it will rise at least another foot (0.3 meters), but possibly as high as 6.6 feet (2 meters) in a high-emissions scenario. Sea level is rising because of added water from melting land ice and the expansion of seawater as it warms.","position":{"start":{"line":134,"column":1},"end":{"line":134,"column":1}},"key":"eGT5VCCR6q"}],"key":"cj5cb0eVSL"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":136,"column":1},"end":{"line":136,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"link","url":"https://science.nasa.gov/climate-change/effects/","position":{"start":{"line":136,"column":1},"end":{"line":136,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Text Source","position":{"start":{"line":136,"column":1},"end":{"line":136,"column":1}},"key":"Y3isemyEbw"}],"urlSource":"https://science.nasa.gov/climate-change/effects/","key":"X1X4kSo7Kc"}],"key":"D0lClq3pGM"}],"key":"ZWV6ntrhZa"}],"key":"p56pfgRJd6"},"references":{"cite":{"order":[],"data":{}}}}